    "| 3 | `voted` | integer | 0 = did not vote, 1 = voted | Binary indicator of self-reported voter turnout. Derived from `f11100rec` (2019/2023) or `f11100r` (2015 CSV variant). Only non-negative values are retained; invalid codes are excluded. |\n",
    "| 4 | `political_interest` | float | 1–4 scale (1 = not at all interested, 4 = very interested); codes −99, −98, 9 treated as missing | Self-reported level of interest in politics. Derived from `f10100`. |\n",
    "| 5 | `trust_avg` | float | Mean of three trust items, each on a scale approximately 1–10; codes −99, −98 treated as missing | Average institutional trust score across three items: trust in the federal government (`f11301`), trust in parliament (`f11302`), and satisfaction with democracy (`f11305`). |\n",
    "| 6 | `demo_satisfaction` | integer | 0 = not satisfied, 1 = satisfied; codes −99, −98, 8, 9 treated as missing | Binary indicator of democratic satisfaction. Derived from `f12010` (original values: 1 → satisfied, 2 → not satisfied). |\n",
    "| 7 | `lr_scale` | float | 1.0–5.0 continuous scale (1 = far left, 5 = far right); codes −99, −98 treated as missing | Left–right self-placement. In 2015: derived from `f12900main7` (7-point scale mapped to 1–5 via fixed mapping). In 2019/2023: derived from `f12900rec` (values 10/20/30/40/50 divided by 10). |\n",
    "\n",
    "The three processed CSVs do not contain a common `survey_year` column; the year dimension is introduced at load time by the pipeline, which reads each file separately and keys the resulting DataFrames by election year (2015, 2019, 2023).\n",
